        function is called, so most pad functions cannot be called
        from within the callback.

        Args:
            unlink: the Gst.PadUnlinkFunction to set.
        """
    def start_task(self, func: TaskFunction) -> _bool:
        """Starts a task that repeatedly calls func with user_data. This function
        is mostly used in pad activation functions to start the dataflow.
        The #GST_PAD_STREAM_LOCK of self will automatically be acquired
        before func is called.

        Args:
            func: the task function to call

        Returns:
            a True if the task could be started.
        """
    def sticky_events_foreach(self, foreach_func: PadStickyEventsForeachFunction) -> None:
        """Iterates all sticky events on self and calls foreach_func for every
        event. If foreach_func returns False the iteration is immediately stopped.

        Args:
            foreach_func: the
                Gst.PadStickyEventsForeachFunction that should be called for every event.
        """
    def stop_task(self) -> _bool:
        """Stop the task of self. This function will also make sure that the
        function executed by the task will effectively stop if not called
        from the GstTaskFunction.

        This function will deadlock if called from the GstTaskFunction of
        the task. Use Gst.Task.pause() instead.

        Regardless of whether the pad has a task, the stream lock is acquired and
        released so as to ensure that streaming through this pad has finished.

        Returns:
            a True if the task could be stopped or False on error.
        """
    def store_sticky_event(self, event: Event) -> FlowReturn:
        """Store the sticky event on self

        Args:
            event: a Gst.Event

        Returns:
            Gst.FlowReturn.OK on success, Gst.FlowReturn.FLUSHING when the pad
                was flushing or Gst.FlowReturn.EOS when the pad was EOS.
